pocket-motion-only: fixes the arithmetic 0014 (a framebuffer that carries alpha) and 0018 (filter layers) added; upstream draws neither a transparent frame nor a filter layer.

0032 — straight-alpha src-over divides by the exact new alpha.

`RgbaTarget::blend` composites a partial source over a partly transparent
destination straight-alpha: the new alpha is `a + da*(255-a)/255`, and the
colour is the premultiplied sum divided back out by it. It divided by the
STORED alpha, rounded to a byte — up to 127/255 below the exact one. That
inflated the colour: by up to half of it at small alphas, and past 255 the
byte wrapped, so white over white came out black. `composite_layer`'s
content-over-shadow step made the same division. Every translucent write
inside a filter layer lands in a transparent buffer, and a glow is a shadow
at offset 0, so translucent white content in a white glow came out as
near-black speckle wherever the rounding went down — the dark dither a film
showed where two translucent white layers overlapped in a `glow-*` node.

Both now divide by `a*255 + da*(255-a)`, 255 times the exact new alpha.
The colour is then a weighted mean of the two inputs and stays between
them; the stored alpha is unchanged. The opaque-destination expression is
untouched, so a frame with a ground is byte-identical outside its filter
layers.

Guards (`engine/core/src/tests.rs`):
`src_over_a_transparent_destination_keeps_the_colour_between_its_inputs`
blends every source alpha over every destination alpha (1..254 each) for
five colour pairs on a one-pixel transparent frame: red before (17,828
composites outside their inputs' range), green after.
`a_translucent_white_over_its_white_glow_stays_white`: every content alpha
at glow gains 0.5, 1 and 2, over a transparent frame and an opaque white
one: red with only the blend fixed (312 not white, the darkest 0), green
with the composite fixed too.
`translucent_whites_overlapping_in_a_glow_never_darken`: two translucent
white boxes (alpha 0.42 and 0.32) overlapping inside a white glow, under an
`overflow-mask` or not, over a dark ground or none: the pair is never
darker than one box alone. Red before onto a transparent destination (507
of 765 darker at one pixel), green after.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: `compositions/filters`
moves — all 30 frames, every changed pixel by exactly one level, all in its
glow, shadow and rack-focus row (frame 15: 4,059 pixels) — the rounding of
the in-layer and content-over-shadow composites. `compositions/alpha` does
not move (its one box is opaque). No other digest and no `visibility` row
moves.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

